// The 4 Layers of Next.js Caching:

// 1. REQUEST MEMOIZATION (Server-side, lasts for exactly ONE page load)
// Solves the "Prop Drilling" problem. Just fetch data wherever you need it.
const data1 = await fetch('url');
const data2 = await fetch('url'); // Instant! Skipped network.

// 2. DATA CACHE (Server-side, lasts FOREVER until you revalidate it)
// fetch('url', { cache: 'force-cache' })

// 3. FULL ROUTE CACHE (Server-side, lasts FOREVER)
// Next.js caches the entire final HTML file output.

// 4. ROUTER CACHE (Client-side, lasts for a few minutes)
// The browser remembers pages you just visited.
// Call `router.refresh()` to bust this cache!
